    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d809">

                <pb facs="0855" n="843" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg843"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.24/1159: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-07-05T16:00:00-04:00">July 5, 1943—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>696. Your 1200, July 3, 6 p.m. You are authorized to exchange notes confirming
                    the Agreement.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d809-f1"/></p>
                <pb facs="0856" n="844" xml:id="pg844"/>
                <p>You may assure the Chileans that the Department will, upon satisfactory
                    completion of Agreement, exert its best efforts to obtain approval of rolling
                    mill and wire drawing machinery. However, no commitment may be given in this
                    connection.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d809-f1" n="12" xml:id="d809-f1-content">
                <p>For text of the Agreement, see note No. 2210, August 11, from the American
                    Ambassador in Chile to the Chilean Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs, <ref
                        target="#pg851">p. 851</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
